      "message": "I\u0027m having a bit of trouble understanding how this works.\n\nHere\u0027s what I think is happening:\n\nSource clock is 8 MHz.  Shift by 3 to get 1 MHz.\n\nTIMER_L is a 24-bit timer counting down at 8 MHz.\n\nWhen the timers are loaded,\nTIMER_L set to ((0xffffffff \u003c\u003c 3) \u0026 0x00ffffff) \u003d 0x00fffff8\nTIMER_H set to (0xffffffff \u003e\u003e 21) \u003d 0x000007ff\n\nWhen reading the timers, go the other direction.  Bottom 21 bits of the 32-bit MHz count come from (TIMER_L\u003e\u003e3) and the top 11 bits come from (TIMER_H\u003c\u003c21).\n\nTIMER_H is a 32-bit timer which counts down when timer_L underflows.\n\nAn interrupt fires when TIMER_H underflows, which reloads the timers.\n\nEvents are handled by a separate 32-bit timer counting down at 8 MHz.\n\n(If that\u0027s correct, a comment saying something like that up at the top of the file would be useful.)",
